	'k09dc794f' => 'Founder Elise Vandamme leads bread instruction, bringing extensive hearth baking mastery to the curriculum since establishing Komugi School in 2014. She mentors students in grain chemistry, dough handling, and classical European bread traditions. Amara Osei directs sourdough and natural fermentation studies, guiding students through starter maintenance, microbial balance, and ambient fermentation timing. Tomás Ferreira leads the viennoiserie bench, instructing students in butter lamination, lamination folding mechanics, and pastry proofing schedules. Each instructor teaches hands-on at the bench, working alongside students through every mix, fold, and bake.',
	'k0a267533' => 'The tuition fee covers all organic flours, butter, dairy, and bakery ingredients consumed throughout the course. Each student also receives a durable linen apron, a professional knife roll outfitted with a curved lame, bench scrapers, and a digital thermometer, alongside the bound Komugi bench book. Tuition also covers the full supervision of the two-week partner kitchen placement following graduation. All listed course fees are stated in euros and include value added tax.',
	'k0ac736c4' => 'Here are clear answers to common questions regarding admissions, tuition fees, course schedules, and daily bench work at Komugi School. For additional inquiries, contact our registry at Hallstraat 14.',
	'k0d97cd7f' => 'Elise Vandamme · Bread',
	'k0e92342a' => 'Lamination baker',
	'k0ec83227' => 'Prospective applicants can attend our open bench mornings held every Saturday from 09:00 to 12:00. These three-hour visits cost €45 and are limited to eight participants to ensure meaningful conversation with faculty. Visitors tour the bakery, observe our baking equipment, inspect dough fermentation stages, and ask detailed questions about the curriculum. Attending an open bench morning satisfies the second stage of our admissions evaluation.',
