	'k14ec2193' => 'Every enrolled student receives a professional equipment kit on their first morning at Hallstraat 14. This kit includes a heavy-duty unbleached linen apron, a professional knife roll containing a curved lame, steel and plastic bench scrapers, and a calibrated digital pocket thermometer. Students also receive the Komugi bench book, a bound operational journal used to document hydration adjustments, ambient bakery temperatures, bake profiles, and formula iterations. All organic flours, cultured dairy, and bakery ingredients used throughout the six weeks are fully covered by the course fee. Students retain all personal tools upon course completion.',
	'k159b20d8' => 'Our teaching bakery is situated at Hallstraat 14, 3011 KD Rotterdam, Netherlands. The school is easily accessible via public transportation, located directly adjacent to the tram 23 stop named Hallstraat, and features dedicated outdoor bicycle racks for daily student use. Practical teaching shifts run Monday through Friday from 06:00 to 14:00, while the administrative office is open for general telephone and in-person inquiries Monday through Friday from 09:00 to 17:00. We ask that visitors schedule appointments in advance to prevent disrupting students during active deck oven loading and dough division.',
	'k17debfdc' => 'The Professional Bread &amp; Pastry programme is an intensive six-week foundation followed by two weeks in an operating partner kitchen. We train twelve students per cohort in the rhythm, discipline, and standards of professional production.',
	'k189bccc4' => 'Butter plasticity, lamination turns and sheeting for croissants, pain au chocolat and brioche.',
	'k1936a279' => 'Week 6',
	'k19730e46' => 'Observations on sourdough hydration, lamination temperatures, and commercial bakery operations written directly by Komugi School instructors and visiting bakers from our partner network.',
	'k1982db1a' => 'Lukas Brenner oversees deck oven baking and production flow, training students in peel handling, thermal recovery, deck loading, and commercial bakery output pacing. Mei-Lin Choi directs classical pastry technique, focusing on enriched doughs, tart shells, seasonal fillings, and precise structural balance. Hanne Jansen manages school admissions and coordinates the bench book curriculum, mentoring students in formula calculation, baker\'s percentages, and technical documentation. Together, our instructors maintain a calm, methodical teaching environment focused entirely on practical competence, kitchen discipline, and repeatable craftsmanship.',
	'k1a7aac51' => 'Short Courses',
	'k1aec1351' => 'A Training Day',
	'k1b604375' => 'Our spacious training floor provides twelve dedicated student bench stations surfaced in solid marble and thick beech wood. Each station is equipped with an individual digital scale, professional dough scrapers, rolling pins, linen proofing couches, and German spruce pulp bannetons. The storeroom maintains organized grain bins and unprinted sacks of regional stone-ground flours, rye, and ancient grains. By limiting cohorts to twelve bakers, every student retains uninterrupted access to their own station, sink, and mixer throughout the daily 06:00 to 14:00 teaching shift.',
	'k1bcca6c7' => 'Hanne Jansen',
	'k1cecfe22' => 'Tuesday centres on laminated doughs: mechanical sheeting, precise butter block temperature and the folds that build honeycomb layers. Croissant and danish doughs are made, rested and cut at the same bench.',
