	'k2d959258' => 'Bread Foundations is an intensive two-week practical course priced at €1,750, designed for cooks and serious amateurs seeking a rigorous commercial grounding. Working Monday through Friday from 06:00 to 14:00, students master direct doughs, preferments, hydration calculations, and hand-shaping disciplines across wheat, rye, and ancient grains. You will learn to control spiral mixing speeds, manage bulk dough fermentation, and bake across multi-deck stone hearth ovens. Class sizes remain capped at twelve students to ensure direct bench supervision from senior instructors throughout every session.',
