	'k589f481c' => 'Assessment at Komugi School is continuous, practical, and grounded in kitchen realities rather than written examinations. Instructors evaluate students daily on dough handling dexterity, temperature management, loaf volume, blister development, and crumb structure during midday critique sessions. Students must demonstrate complete mastery of the forty core formulas recorded in their bench books and maintain tidy, efficient workstation discipline. Speed, sanitation, and consistency under production pressure form the core criteria for completing the six-week syllabus. There are no theoretical multiple-choice tests; proof of competence rests solely in the quality of the loaves pulled from the deck.',
	'k59281ab6' => 'The admissions process comprises four distinct steps. First, prospective students submit an online application outlining their background and career goals. Second, candidates attend a Saturday open bench morning to meet our faculty and tour the bakery. Third, successful applicants receive a formal written offer within ten days of their visit. Fourth, the student confirms enrollment by paying a fifty percent deposit, with the remaining balance due prior to the start of instruction.',
