	'k5f25a222' => 'Mon–Fri',
	'k5f933376' => 'At 10:00, the bakery shifts into high gear as doughs reach optimal bench proof and division begins. Students portion batches with bench scrapers, pre-shape rounds, rest them on wooden surfaces, and perform final shaping into baskets and linen couches. By 12:00, the deck ovens are saturated at 250°C, and loading starts using long wooden peels and controlled steam injection. At 13:00, students assemble for the daily critique, cutting open selected loaves to inspect crumb gelatinization, aeration, and crust caramelization. The day concludes at 13:30 with full station clean-down, equipment sanitation, and bench book formula logging.',
	'k616eb0fc' => 'By 06:00 the deck ovens are at 250°C. Bakers move between spiral mixers, proofing racks, and wooden benches under soft morning light, turning raw grain, water, and salt into daily production before the surrounding city begins its day.',
