	'k872e5e4d' => 'Commercial baking demands physical stamina and acute awareness of environmental fluctuations. During weeks five and six, students experience modified production schedules that simulate realistic early morning and overnight baker shifts. This training teaches bakers to adapt fermentation timing when flour shipments vary or ambient barometric pressure changes during the early morning hours. Working through these pacing challenges prepares students to enter professional partner kitchens with the confidence to manage commercial deck ovens, maintain speed during peak loading cycles, and troubleshoot dough irregularities without hesitating.',
