	'k88479e61' => 'The bakery floor opens at 06:00 sharp with a fifteen-minute briefing led by the day\'s bench instructor. Students review the daily production sheet, check overnight dough retarding temperatures, and begin scaling base ingredients on digital scales. By 07:30, mixing begins in our four spiral mixers, balancing water temperature and mechanical friction to reach precise dough targets. Bulk fermentation follows immediately in temperature-controlled tubs, where students execute scheduled folds and monitor fermentation progress through sensory and volumetric observation. This quiet morning window establishes the structural foundation and hydration schedule for the day\'s entire bake.',
