	'k8c6f92f3' => 'Bread Foundations',
	'k8c7aec39' => 'Upon receiving a written offer of admission, applicants must submit a fifty percent deposit within ten days to secure their place in the cohort. The remaining balance must be paid in full prior to the first day of class. Because each cohort is limited to twelve students, deposits ensure committed enrollment and allow us to allocate bench stations, personal tool rolls, and raw materials accurately.',
	'k8c85e761' => 'The second half of the course builds technical precision and commercial bakery speed. Week four covers laminated doughs, focusing on butter temper, lamination turns, sheeting consistency, and proofing control for viennoiserie. In week five, students take control of production scheduling and our four-deck ovens, learning steam delivery, thermal recovery, and peeling techniques under live commercial conditions. Week six is dedicated to placement preparation and the final comprehensive bake, where each student manages an entire production run independently from scaling to oven clearance. This final week prepares bakers directly for their transition into professional partner kitchens.',
	'k8f1becd5' => 'Viennoiserie Week',
	'k8f3ebe6f' => 'Hallstraat 14, 3011 KD Rotterdam, Netherlands',
	'k8f49c208' => 'Rotterdam',
	'k8f8dd547' => 'Dough temperature',
	'k8f9da0bd' => 'Tuition covers all ingredients, personal tool rolls, uniforms, and placement supervision. We offer six focused courses ranging from our three-hour open bench sessions to the six-week Professional Bread &amp; Pastry course. Each cohort is strictly capped at twelve participants, with two part-fee bursary places per cohort.',
	'k8fc5e80e' => 'We offer two distinct five-day intensive courses for specialized craft mastery. Viennoiserie Week, priced at €980, explores laminated dough production, covering butter plasticity, lamination turns, mechanical sheeting, and proofing control for croissants, pain au chocolat, and brioche. Sourdough Week, priced at €920, focuses entirely on natural levain systems, wild yeast propagation, lactic versus acetic fermentation balances, and stone-ground flour hydration. Both five-day modules run full-time from 06:00 to 14:00, giving students immersive hands-on repetition on commercial bakery equipment.',
	'k90fa2ae3' => 'What you carry out of the door',
	'k912b7eca' => 'Bench book',
	'k929de03d' => 'Monday begins at 06:00 with flour chemistry, digital scaling, water temperature calculation and the first dough mixing. Students weigh every batch twice and learn why a two-degree swing changes the whole morning.',
