	'kb45dbd3d' => 'The first three weeks establish foundational hand skills and grain science at the wooden bench. In week one, students focus on flour, water, and salt, analyzing hydration rates, ash content, and dough development through manual mixing and temperature tracking. Week two transitions into wild fermentation and sourdough management, examining starter vitality, fermentation rates, and acidity control across varying ambient temperatures. During week three, the focus centers on shaping and scoring, where students master repetitive bench shaping for boules, bâtards, and baguettes on linen couches. Every student handles individual batches daily to build physical consistency and tactile judgment before progressing into enriched formulas.',
