	'kc3fad45f' => 'Saturday Open Bench Mornings',
	'kc439cbe7' => 'Viennoiserie',
	'kc4437c44' => 'Weekend Bench is a two-day weekend course held on Saturday and Sunday, priced at €320. Tailored for dedicated home bakers and working professionals unable to attend weekday classes, this workshop demystifies long-fermentation hearth bread in a professional bakery environment. Students learn sourdough starter maintenance, dough autolysis, gentle coil folding, bench pre-shaping, banneton proofing, and scoring techniques using professional deck ovens. Participants leave with active levain cultures, detailed formula cards, and the bread baked over the course of the weekend.',
	'kc5c8d3f5' => 'We host open bench mornings every Saturday from 09:00 to 12:00 for prospective applicants and bread enthusiasts. Priced at €45 per attendee, each session is strictly limited to eight places to ensure an intimate, conversational experience. Participants tour our deck ovens and proofing rooms, observe dough handling techniques, handle grain samples, and discuss course details directly with faculty members. Attending an open bench morning satisfies stage two of our admissions process and provides an honest look at the physical daily rhythms of commercial bakery training.',
	'kc79f0595' => 'The heart of our baking floor consists of three commercial four-deck ovens and one rotating rack oven. The four-deck stone hearth ovens deliver continuous high-temperature heat distribution with independent digital steam injection across every deck, allowing students to bake crusty levain loaves under precise vapor saturation. The single rack oven provides convection airflow control for consistent baking of viennoiserie, brioche, and enriched pastries on multi-tier bakery racks. Students learn to load, steam, vent, and unload both oven types daily, mastering peel ergonomics and heat management under authentic commercial bakery pressures.',
